  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "A regular dodecagon (\\(12\\) sides) is inscribed in a circle with radius \\(r\\) inches. The area of the dodecagon, in square inches, is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(3r^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2r^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{3r^2\\sqrt3}{4}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(r^2\\sqrt3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(3r^2\\sqrt3\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1962-p18.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Each of the \\(12\\) central triangles has area \\[ \\frac12r^2\\sin30^\\circ=\\frac{r^2}{4}. \\] Their total area is \\(12(\\frac{r^2}{4})=3r^2.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Divide the dodecagon into \\(12\\) triangles with vertex at the center",
        "Each central angle is \\(30^\\circ\\), so use \\(\\frac12r^2\\sin30^\\circ\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
